    "bio": "Radha Yadav, born on April 21, 2000, in Kandivli (West), Mumbai, is an Indian international cricketer renowned for her left-arm orthodox spin. She made her T20I debut for India against South Africa on February 13, 2018. Primarily a bowler, she is also considered a bowling all-rounder due to her right-handed batting and exceptional fielding. Yadav has been a consistent performer in the T20I format, notably becoming the second Indian woman to achieve 100 T20I wickets. Her career highlights include being the joint-leading wicket-taker for India in the 2018 ICC Women's World Twenty20 and contributing to the team's runner-up finish in the 2020 ICC Women's T20 World Cup.",
